  "title": "utilpeek: macro snapshot (US Treasury yield curve, ECB FX rates, dollar-index proxy)"
 },
 "description": "utilpeek: Use when an agent needs the rates backdrop before a market decision: Treasury yields, SOFR/EFFR, FX, oil and gas in one call. For the Treasury curve on a past date use treasury_yield_curve. Returns one macro snapshot: US Treasury par yield curve with spreads, ECB euro rates, a dollar-index proxy from them (not the ICE index), EFFR and SOFR (New York Fed), WTI, Brent and Henry Hub spot (US EIA, if configured); each section has source, as-of date and licence. VIX, equity indices and gold are not included (`not_included`); commodities are null (`not_configured`) without an EIA key. A failed source is listed in `sources_failed`, section null; all failing is a 503 (not charged). Informational only, not investment advice. Typically under 0.2 s from cache; up to about 30 s when the slow Treasury feed is fetched. Price: USD 0.004. Free: 10 utilpeek calls per IP per UTC day. Docs: https://tanod.dev/learn/macro-snapshot-api.html",
